WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.740
- [Narrator] For the last five years,

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.350
New York's LaGuardia Airport

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.340
has been undergoing an $8 billion upgrade.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.260
And according to the Port
Authority of New York

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.093
and New Jersey,

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:13.030
its transformation will
be complete next spring.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.110
- The old airport,

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.050
which was probably one of
the most hated airports

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.230
in the country will have been transformed

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.437
into one of the best.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:22.620
- [Narrator] But rebuilding
an entire airport

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.810
while keeping it functional
for up to 50,000 passengers

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.160
on busy days is no easy feat.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.290
So how did the Port Authority pull it off

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.410
and what can travelers
expect going forward?

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.060
Renovating LaGuardia Airport
involved tearing down

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.750
and rebuilding every
single passenger facility

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.520
with the exception of the
landmark Marine Air Terminal.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.640
And since it remained an active airport,

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.950
renovations had to be
done one area at a time.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.974
- The construction pattern had to be

00:00:48.974 --> 00:00:52.453
that you build a new passenger facility.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.170
You put that into use

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.270
and it was then, and only then

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.010
that you could tear down the old.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.570
- [Narrator] The pandemic
brought challenges,

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.260
such as having to enforce
strict safety protocols

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.160
for workers on the construction project.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.680
But the drop in passengers
did make it easier

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.970
to construct new roadways.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.120
- You could actually confine the traffic

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.930
to individual lanes

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:18.060
so that construction on the
new terminals could accelerate

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.150
because you could use those for cranes,

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.130
for other construction equipment.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.770
- [Narrator] The Port
Authority says the airport

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.170
is currently about halfway
through renovations,

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.160
and so far, there have been
some positive reactions.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.747
- We've heard from pilots,
we've heard from airline staff.

00:01:31.747 --> 00:01:35.620
I've actually been in the airport

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.960
when passengers come out of a jet way

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.330
having just got off of a plane

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.970
where they do a complete double take

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.700
and say, "Did I get on
the wrong airplane?"

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.840
- [Narrator] Terminal B is 90% finished,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.790
and features art, greenery,
four airline lounges

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:54.350
and 42 new shops and restaurants.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.710
The Port Authority says
that one key difference

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.700
between the old and new Terminal B

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.820
is that almost all of
the shops and restaurants

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.560
are located after security,

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.500
so travelers can shop and dine

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.950
while waiting for their flights.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:06.970
There's also a sky bridge

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:10.870
that allows passengers to
walk over active taxi ways.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.520
- As you drive up to the airport

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.940
on the departures level,

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.050
you will see an extraordinary vista

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.010
of the Manhattan skyline.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.780
There's one brand new concourse,

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.300
which is quite striking.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.150
It looks out both on Flushing
Bay and on City Field.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.810
- [Narrator] Terminal
C, which is being built

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.950
by Delta Airlines is
set to open next spring.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.590
All of the new passenger facilities

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.030
have also moved closer
to the main highway.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.580
This way, aircrafts
have more space to taxi

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.720
and there could be fewer
issues getting to their gate.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.960
- Now we're seeing an airport emerge,

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.190
which is what the region deserves,

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.620
what travelers deserve,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.430
what employees of all of the employers

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.943
at the airport deserve.

00:02:53.943 --> 00:02:56.526
(lively music)

